module

public import Sheaf.Paper.PurityRelativeKummerMaps

/-! # A component of the relative Kummer calculation

Source: blueprint sk-prop-a1-kummer, prop-pur-gm-relative-kummer.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry

namespace WeilConjectures.PurityFiniteSetting

attribute [local irreducible] ProEtale.upperStar ProEtale.lowerStar
  Functor.leftDerivedFunctor Functor.rightDerivedFunctor
  ProEtale.derivedUpperStarLowerStarAdjunction ProEtale.derivedBaseChangeMap
  constantPullback twistPullback derivedCoefficientPullback relativeUnit kummerGenerator
  constant twist constantEtale twistEtale coordinateKummer


/-- The degree-zero unit and coordinate Kummer section on the punctured line are
isomorphisms, and higher direct images above degree one vanish.
Source: blueprint prop-pur-gm-relative-kummer, proof steps 1--9 and 13--15
(blueprint: lem-pur-relative-punctured-cohomology).

Proof: Put r = ell^(level/e). If r=1, the finite-level identity rA=0 makes A zero;
all the displayed objects are zero and all assertions follow. Otherwise the exponent
level/e is positive. The Kummer sequence on Gm over k and Pic(Gm)=0 identify H1 with units modulo
r-th powers. Laurent units are uniquely a*t^n; k-units are r-divisible, so this
quotient is Z/r generated by the actual boundary of t. Constant sections give H0,
and affine-curve cohomological dimension gives vanishing above one. Finite free
extension from Z/r to A preserves this boundary. At a geometric stalk of Y, the
strict-henselization formula and the rotated smooth-base-change square identify the
cohomology with this calculation over k. Derived direct-image composition identifies
that isomorphism with restriction, which carries t to t. The presheaf description of
higher direct images identifies its edge section with the germ of the same class.
Stalk conservativity gives the two specified isomorphisms and the vanishing.
Exact etale/pro-etale comparison, the canonical counit mate, and comparison of edge
sections transport these precise maps. The comparison on global cohomology is the
unit-induced comparison defining coordinateKummer, by evaluation at the final object
and the natural scalar-forgetting comparison. No finite-type condition on Y is used. -/
theorem relative_punctured_cohomology (P : PurityFiniteSetting.{u})
    (h : P.ramificationIndex ∣ P.level) (Y : Scheme.{u})
    (a : Y ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of P.field.k)) :
    IsIso ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor
      (Sheaf (Scheme.ProEt.topology Y) (ModuleCat.{u + 1} P.Coefficient)) 0).map
        (P.relativeUnit h (puncturedProjection Y) true)) ∧
    IsIso (P.kummerGenerator h Y a) ∧
    ∀ (m : ℕ), 2 ≤ m → IsZero
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor
        (Sheaf (Scheme.ProEt.topology Y) (ModuleCat.{u + 1} P.Coefficient)) (m : ℤ)).obj
          ((ProEtale.lowerStar (ModuleCat.{u + 1} P.Coefficient)
            (puncturedProjection Y)).rightDerivedFunctor.obj
              (P.derivedSheaf h (Punctured Y) true))) := by sorry

end WeilConjectures.PurityFiniteSetting
